elements.definition:
The infant is considered to have good attachment if all four of the following signs are present:
- more areola seen above the infant’s top lip than below the bottom lip;
- mouth wide open;
- lower lip turned outwards;
- chin touching the breast.

The child has one or more medical complications of severe acute malnutrition:
- any general danger sign;
- any severe classification;
- pneumonia​, persistent diarrhoea​, dysentery​, malaria, measles;
- oedema of both feet.
